From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 6Xkljk8Vj7Tk1k4 <6Xkljk8Vj7Tk1k4@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:48:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gta4xl-common: sepolicy: Let SurfaceFlinger read
 vendor.display props

LineageOS' SurfaceFlinger reads vendor.display.vds_allow_hwc in
SurfaceFlinger::init() (HWC for virtual/WFD displays, a QCOM display
property). device/samsung_slsi/sepolicy maps the vendor.display. prefix
to vendor_hwc_prop (next to our own vendor.hwc. entry) without granting
SurfaceFlinger read access, so every boot logs

  avc: denied { read } for comm="surfaceflinger"
  name="u:object_r:vendor_hwc_prop:s0" dev="tmpfs"
  scontext=u:r:surfaceflinger:s0 tcontext=u:object_r:vendor_hwc_prop:s0
  tclass=file permissive=0

The property is never set on this device, so the read returning the
default (false) and the denied read behave the same: no user-visible
impact, present on the lineage-23.2 baseline too.

vendor_hwc_prop is a vendor_restricted_prop, which coredomain may be
granted read access to (only set is neverallowed), and this mirrors
get_prop(surfaceflinger, vendor_display_prop) in the QCOM policies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sepolicy/vendor/surfaceflinger.te | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sepolicy/vendor/surfaceflinger.te b/sepolicy/vendor/surfaceflinger.te
index 30a731e..549a326 100644
--- a/sepolicy/vendor/surfaceflinger.te
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/surfaceflinger.te
@@ -1,3 +1,7 @@
 r_dir_file(surfaceflinger, hal_graphics_composer_default);
 
 allow surfaceflinger unlabeled:filesystem getattr;
+
+# vendor.display.vds_allow_hwc, read in SurfaceFlinger::init(); the
+# vendor.display. prefix is vendor_hwc_prop (device/samsung_slsi/sepolicy)
+get_prop(surfaceflinger, vendor_hwc_prop)
